    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0521" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/118: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-20T14:00:00-05:00">October 20, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>71. Consul Pernambuco inquired October 18<anchor n="7" xml:id="d455-f1"/> whether
                    local <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> revolutionary Government should be
                    informed regarding forthcoming visit to that port of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pensacola</hi> and whether customary official call on Governor should be
                    arranged for under existing circumstances. Department in reply instructed Consul
                    to inform <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Government of visit to
                    Pernambuco but stated that official calls should not be made to revolutionary
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
